{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"d542a85782a85e66","type":"group","x":-1099,"y":-625,"width":1355,"height":1450,"label":"Flow with Learning Processes"},
		{"id":"d2073ad585888b69","type":"group","x":341,"y":-412,"width":759,"height":1237,"label":"Principles for Efficiency"},
		{"id":"a669c531ac3a6410","type":"text","text":"# Attention Gateway","x":-1079,"y":-605,"width":320,"height":50},
		{"id":"6d175942cc0701ca","type":"text","text":"# Encoding Gateway","x":-659,"y":-605,"width":320,"height":50},
		{"id":"a4c10d64b9488346","type":"text","text":"# Focus","x":-1044,"y":-392,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"349b5c378379f981","type":"text","text":"# FER-MO","x":-409,"y":-825,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"dc379051f5a76f67","type":"text","text":"# Storage via Retrieval Gateway","x":-284,"y":-605,"width":520,"height":50},
		{"id":"7bc804010441704c","type":"text","text":"### During Learning (Within a Topic)\n\n- Read for 1-2 minutes\n- Perform Metacognition in the process.\n- Recall new content onto mind map.","x":-147,"y":-203,"width":250,"height":318},
		{"id":"7e72df4b4116dd91","type":"text","text":"# Retrieval","x":-147,"y":-392,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6c7d595c8dbda713","type":"text","text":"# Encoding","x":-625,"y":-392,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f6ff44c2e2696761","type":"text","text":"### After a Topic\n- Grab a new sheet of paper.\n- Rebuild mind map from memory\n- DOESN'T HAVE TO BE ACCURATE.\n- Organize content and relationships in a better SCHEMA.","x":-147,"y":164,"width":250,"height":334},
		{"id":"96e79bc6595694c0","type":"text","text":"### External\n- Remove Environmental Distractions\n- Clean up clutter and workspace.","x":-1044,"y":-301,"width":250,"height":193},
		{"id":"7adfd032356071b5","type":"text","text":"# Metacognition","x":407,"y":-392,"width":267,"height":60},
		{"id":"e0d8a8fcc5933144","type":"text","text":"### Internal\n- Pray\n- 5 Deep Breaths\n- Clear the mind","x":-1044,"y":-75,"width":250,"height":150},
		{"id":"6056f5f723d3ef0b","type":"text","text":"### Preliminary\n- Skim over proceeding topics.\n- Ask questions, create hypothesis, and make predictions.\n- Get a \"lay of the land.\"","x":-1044,"y":118,"width":250,"height":267},
		{"id":"7810371864329ee8","type":"text","text":"### Mind mapping\n- Design to force the brain into building relationships and connections.\n- ITS SUPPOSED TO BE MESSY","x":-625,"y":-203,"width":250,"height":248},
		{"id":"dc6084e5875a4e9b","type":"text","text":"### G.R.I.N.D.E (Justin Sung)\n\n- Think about\n\t- Grouping\n\t- Relationships\n\t- Interconnected\n\t- Non-Verbal\n\t- Directional\n\t- Emphasized\n- Do this while **encoding**.\n\nIncreases cognitive load, promote proper encoding, creates more direction for a better mind map.\n\n","x":416,"y":-301,"width":250,"height":465},
		{"id":"7002bad6ff8bb21c","type":"text","text":"### General Metacognition\n\n- Ask questions\n- Formulate synthesis.\n- Make predictions.\n- Do this while **conducting preliminary** and **encoding**.","x":416,"y":210,"width":250,"height":288},
		{"id":"a4bc786a48d88cc9","type":"text","text":"# Organization","x":796,"y":-392,"width":246,"height":60},
		{"id":"b01da8a1762090f0","type":"text","text":"### Time Management\n- Work in blocks of 45 minutes.\n- Take 10 minute breaks.\n- Avoid doom scrolling or anything **dopamine heavy** during breaks.","x":793,"y":-274,"width":250,"height":319},
		{"id":"80708070c75c2d7c","type":"text","text":"### Recommendations (Justin Sung)\n\n- Mind mapping is a skill.\n- Skill takes progress.\n- Focus on building each step of the process **one at a time**.","x":796,"y":210,"width":250,"height":319},
		{"id":"6566146f2d753ac6","type":"text","text":"### Metacognition - G.R.I.N.D.E (Justin Sung)\n- Keep in mind:\n\t- Grouping\n\t- Relationships\n\t- Interconnected\n\t- Non-Verbal\n\t- Directional\n\t- Emphasized\n- Keys for good mind-mapping and encoding.","x":-625,"y":115,"width":250,"height":380},
		{"id":"74c0a3cd460ccaf6","x":-625,"y":529,"width":250,"height":244,"type":"text","text":"### Depth of Asking Questions\n- When forming relationships.\n- Ask questions.\n- This creates retention, detail, and depth."},
		{"id":"fee45db6b63fbea4","x":-1044,"y":412,"width":250,"height":388,"type":"text","text":"### Working on G - Grouping\n- Focus on creating groups\n- Read a section and find the main idea.\n- Allow the details to spill outward.\n- Allow relationships and cross-grouping to bring together topics."}
	],
